<speak>
<break time="2s"/>
<mark name="b1_alert"/>
A security engineer gets a C V E alert late Friday afternoon — cross-site scripting in react-router, a library in nearly every modern web app.
<break time="1500ms"/>
<mark name="b2_question"/>
They need to know, right now, which applications in the portfolio are affected, and in what order to patch.
<break time="1500ms"/>
<mark name="b3_depth"/>
For this question they don't need reasoning — they need coverage. They bump the depth from 5 to 30: pull every package manifest, every lockfile, across every repo.
<break time="2s"/>
<mark name="b4_search"/>
OutcomeOps runs a portfolio-wide retrieval. Thirty semantically-matched documents surface — package files, lockfiles, dependency graphs — all from the knowledge base.
<break time="1500ms"/>
<mark name="b5_found"/>
Three applications have react-router installed. OutcomeOps identifies the version running in each.
<break time="1500ms"/>
<mark name="b6_vuln"/>
Two are on vulnerable releases — version 7.11 and 7.10. The third needs manual verification.
<break time="2s"/>
<mark name="b7_priority"/>
The response ranks them by impact. The customer-facing portal patches first — user sessions, uploads, billing data on the line. Analytics second. The internal tool gets verified before close of day.
<break time="1500ms"/>
<mark name="b8_commands"/>
Each priority comes with the exact upgrade command. Ready to copy, execute, and merge.
<break time="1500ms"/>
<mark name="b9_OI"/>
Thirty matches across every repo. Three apps identified. A patch plan ready to merge. This is organizational intelligence — your code, everywhere, queryable in plain language.
<break time="2s"/>
</speak>
